Package: link
Title: Intrinsic Habitat Potential and Fish Passage Connectivity for Stream
    Networks
Version: 0.65.0
Date: 2026-10-14
Authors@R: c(
    person("Allan", "Irvine", , "al@newgraphenvironment.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3495-2128")),
    person("Simon", "Norris", role = "ctb"),
    person("New Graph Environment Ltd.", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Models where fish habitat could be on a stream network and
    whether fish can reach it. For each species it classifies stream, lake
    and wetland reaches as spawning or rearing habitat from gradient and
    channel width or discharge. It resolves which reaches each species can
    reach past falls and steep gradients, using fish observations and
    habitat confirmations as evidence of passage, and records the road
    and rail crossings and dams below each reach. Every rule and threshold is a
    row in a config bundle, and every run records its inputs, so a result
    traces back to the rule that produced it. Runs on the British Columbia
    Freshwater Atlas through 'fresh'. Experimental: APIs and outputs
    change without notice.
